Tor 0.4.6.10 — PREMATURE_DATA real-attack (v2: stream-attach hook + marker)
Files: src/core/or/circuituse.c (Tor patch) + experiments/shadow_harness.mjs (parser)
Model: modified (malicious) client, env-gated (TOR_FSM_ATTACK_PREMATURE_DATA), benign by default.

WHY v1 FAILED
  v1 hooked circuit_finish_handshake (first hop) and looked for an AP stream in
  AP_CONN_STATE_CIRCUIT_WAIT. In this Shadow run Tor keeps a pool of pre-built
  OPEN circuits, so a stream is essentially never WAITING at first-hop-completion
  time => the hook found no stream and fired ~0 times (begins 30≈31, no delta).
  Also the begin log line carries the n_circ_id (channel id, ~2.8e9), NOT the
  global_identifier the parser keys on, so it could not be attributed correctly.

v2 DESIGN
  Tor patch (circuituse.c, connection_ap_handshake_attach_circuit, general-conn
  branch, immediately BEFORE circuit_get_open_circ_or_launch):
    When env set and the stream is a CONNECT stream not yet on a circuit, scan
    circuit_get_global_list() for an ORIGIN, CIRCUIT_STATE_BUILDING, PURPOSE
    C_GENERAL circuit whose first hop (cpath) is CPATH_STATE_OPEN. If found:
      link_apconn_to_circ(conn, foc, foc->cpath);   // first (OPEN) hop
      log_info(LD_CIRC, "TOR_FSM_PREMATURE_BEGIN gid=%u", foc->global_identifier);
      connection_ap_handshake_send_begin(conn);      // GENUINE RELAY_BEGIN early
      return 1;
    Otherwise fall through to normal attach (no premature that time).
  This sends a REAL begin cell down a half-built circuit (first hop open, circuit
  not yet OPEN) and logs the circuit's GLOBAL id — the same id origin_circuit_new
  logs and the parser keys on. Honest: the marker records a real action + real id.

  Safety: link_apconn_to_circ is in the same file (static, callable). We bypass
  connection_ap_handshake_attach_chosen_circuit (which asserts state==OPEN) by
  calling link + send_begin directly. assert_circ_anonymity_ok only asserts on
  onehop_tunnel; a general 3-hop circuit skips it. cpath first hop is OPEN so
  crypto is ready and connection_edge_send_command succeeds.

  Parser (shadow_harness.mjs):
    - new vars: lastReadyCircuitId, pendingPrematureGid
    - on last-hop RECV_EXTENDED push: lastReadyCircuitId = cid  (circuit now READY)
    - on marker line "TOR_FSM_PREMATURE_BEGIN gid=N": pendingPrematureGid = N
    - on begin line "connection_ap_handshake_send_begin(): Sending relay cell":
        cid = pendingPrematureGid || lastReadyCircuitId || lastCircuitId
        (marker -> BUILDING circ -> PREMATURE_DATA; otherwise -> READY -> valid)
      begin regex narrowed to the "Sending relay cell" line so each begin counts
      once (the old /send_begin\(\)/ matched BOTH that and the "Address/port sent"
      line, double-counting).

  Net effect (expected): benign PREMATURE_DATA ~0 (FPR fixed); attack
  PREMATURE_DATA = number of genuine early begins forced onto building circuits.

  NOTE: hit count is timing-dependent (needs a building circuit with first hop
  open at stream-attach time). If too low, escalate to a forcing variant (make the
  stream wait for a building circuit instead of taking an open one).

